  {
   "id": "grief_loss.explain.001",
   "kind": "explain",
   "stage": ["explore"],
   "text": {
    "en": "Grief comes in waves. It can bring sadness, anger, numbness, guilt, even relief. All of that can be normal. It often softens with time and support."
   },
   "ageBand": ["adult"],
   "tags": ["grief", "normal"],
   "triggers": ["am i normal", "is this normal"],
   "doNotSay": [],
   "sources": [
    {"type": "background", "section": "RES_H1 10.6", "note": "Grief is a normal response that usually eases with time and support; prolonged or disabling grief should go to a clinician. General teaching; no source opened; clinician to confirm."}
   ],
   "evidenceLevel": "C",
   "risk": "low",
   "askPermission": true,
   "needsScholarReview": false,
   "needsClinicianReview": true,
   "needsNativeClinicianReview": false,
   "reviewedBy": null,
   "reviewedOn": null,
   "status": "draft"
  },
  {
   "id": "grief_loss.explain.002",
   "kind": "explain",
   "stage": ["explore"],
   "text": {
    "en": "Many people replay what they could have done differently. It's part of grief, and it is a sign of how much you cared. It doesn't mean it was your fault."
   },
   "ageBand": ["adult"],
   "tags": ["grief", "guilt"],
   "triggers": ["if only", "i should have"],
   "doNotSay": [],
   "sources": [
